  "plot": "Rachel Watson clings to the wreckage of her identity by self-medicating with cheap vodka and voyeurism. Her daily transit offers a window into a life she no longer possesses, fixating on a neighborhood blonde who represents everything Rachel has lost. This obsession curdles into a frantic, disjointed nightmare when she witnesses a perceived betrayal. Driven by a surge of righteous, drunken fury, she descends into a mental fog that swallows the events of a single, violent evening. She awakens battered and stained with blood. Haunted by the void in her memory and the news of a local disappearance, Rachel weaponizes her own instability, choosing to trust her fractured instincts over the terrifying reality of her mounting cognitive rot.",
